with the chairman of the House Judiciary  and oversight committees are now making  a request for a second special council  that formal request was made about an  hour ago with the Attorney General jeff  Sessions in a Fox News exclusive tonight  the two chairmen are with me now Bob  Goodlatte from the House Judiciary  Committee and trey Gowdy from the House  Oversight Committee and gentlemen thank  you for your time here  chairman Gowdy you sledder States  matters have arisen what's changed what  changed for me was the knowledge that  there two dozen witnesses that Michael  Horowitz the Inspector General would not  have access to so your options are DOJ  investigated themselves they can't do  that because of conflict of interest let  the Inspector General do it now I'm a  big fan of my coral woods but he has no  jurisdiction over witnesses that if  either left the department or never  worked there so when I counted up 24  witnesses that he would not be able to  access where he to investigated yeah  only one conclusion that special counsel  who's on that list  everybody from Jim Comey - Andy McCabe -  rebecky my Sidney Blumenthal Cody  Shearer anyone who no longer works for  the Department of Justice over the FBI  State Department you may recall a couple  of weeks ago there was some indication  that State Department employees were  feeding information diffusion GPS they  would be outside the reach of the  Inspector General so anyone who's not  currently employee of DOJ Michael  Horowitz doesn't have subpoena poverty  there was a report that McCabe was a  leaker for the Hillary Clinton matter is  that true I don't know  and Horowitz will be issuing that report  and I have a lot of confidence in him  then I think bill he's a straight  shooter and we'll see - chairman  Goodlatte you said earlier today about  the FISA Court specifically the process  was abused how well it was abused by a  gathering of information from a very  suspect source not disclosing that  information to the court and in my  opinion getting authority to look into  the background of an American citizen  life on questionable circumstances and  that is a very serious concern you know  the FBI is  America's premier law-enforcement  organization every day thousands and  thousands of great men and women keep us  safe investigate crime prevent terrorist  attacks but several people at the top of  this organization have engaged in  activities that are questionable and I  think that in order to set the record  straight clear what is going on at the  FBI and make sure this does not happen  again we need to have an outside special  counseling mr. let me read from your  letter in part on screen you write  there's evidence of bias trending toward  animus in your letter among those  charged with investigating serious cases  there is evidence political opposition  research was used in court filings  there's evidence this political  opposition research was neither vetted  before it was used nor fully revealed to  relevant tribunal and quote do you have  evidence the Department of Justice was  spying on the Trump team during the  election that depends on whether or not  you consider Carter phase to be part of  the Trump team he was an advisor to this  so to the extent that he was an advisor  absolutely this whole FISA warrant was  on quarter page and and necessarily you  would also pick up conversations that  quarter-page was having with others so  the answer that question de facto is yes  when you will prove the warrant against  quarter-page mm-hmm do you agree I agree  its premise ton the idea that mr. Page  was somehow critically involved in  something that they wanted to  investigate and I think the case that  was built for that is highly suspect  what is wrong with the IG doing his job  there's nothing wrong with the IG doing  his job and I want him to go ahead he  has a couple of tasks in front of him  one is to complete his investigation  into how the FBI handled the Clinton  email matter that is separate and we  want that report out as soon as possible  because we know he's been working hard  on that he's looked at more than a  million documents and that should be  made public the Attorney General has now  tasked him with looking into this matter  as well but has as trey has noted he  can't do the complete job it involves  other departments of the government  do you trust the Attorney General I  definitely welcome the Attorney General  encouraging that aspect of the  investigation I think more needs to be  done and I think the way to do that that  helps the Attorney General the Deputy  Attorney General the Department of  Justice and the FBI is to take it  outside of those organizations so the  American people can see this properly  investigated those looking on the other  side of this may suggest that Congress  can go ahead and do this job what's  wrong with that idea anyone who's  watched Congress over the last 12 months  we leak like subs and us a week only  because I'm a member of Congress but  that's pretty common for this town yeah  it is but serious investigations don't  leave the executive branch  investigations whether it's your local  district attorney or whether it's Bob  Muller there are far fewer leaks from  Bob Mulder than there are from Adam  Schiff  so we don't have the tools we don't have  access to a grand jury we can't grant  immunity we can't compel testimony and  we're not we don't prosecute crime so  there are a thousand reasons to let the  executive branch or Special Counsel  handle this as opposed to Congress you  do know where special counsels lead you  start with a land deal in Arkansas and  you end up with a blue dress you have no  control over that you can set the  strictures of the jurisdiction if  Attorney General Sessions decides to  appoint special counsel he's going to  give a document that sets the  jurisdiction the only reason Bob Muller  can go where he's going now with manna  fort and others is because the fourth  Clause of that jurisdiction allows him  to pursue other matters that may arise  so you can you can limit the  jurisdiction in the four corners of the  document there was a suggestion today  that if the house flips in November you  would lose control of the issue is that  part of the reason why you're pursuing  it now Jana no I don't think we're going  to lose control of the house but I think  that control of this investigation has  to be done in a more orderly fashion  than you get when it becomes a political  football as this issue clearly has in  the House Intelligence Committee and  elsewhere in the Congress so we're going  to continue to do our oversight duties  to investigate but I think a more  thorough investigation that can get to  the bottom of the matter and do it in a  way that can result in the FBI's  reputation being restored and changes  that are needed to be made be made is  best done with the web minute counsel  when will you get a response in your  letter from the Attorney General we  don't know but we hope we hear from him  soon and we hope that he takes action  and that he does so in a substantive way  will you get an answer I don't know that  we'll get a formal answer the fact that  he doesn't appoint one I guess is an  answer he doesn't owe us a formal  explanation but I think it'd be wise for  him to give us one because I I think our  you know chairman Goodlatte and I do not  routinely call for special counsel I've  resisted to call in other cases this  fact pattern is unique and compelling  and I think you ought to really consider  it gentlemen thank you for your time sir  trey Gowdy Bob Goodlatte  thank you

